From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.media.devices: factory IInspectable, audio selectors, default-device events

The FIXME stubs of the DLL, done as Windows behaves:

- the MediaDevice factory's GetIids, GetTrustLevel and GetRuntimeClassName;
  ActivateInstance stays E_NOTIMPL (a static class); an unknown IID is
  E_NOINTERFACE without a FIXME.
- GetAudioCaptureSelector, GetAudioRenderSelector and GetVideoCaptureSelector
  return the device interface class queries
  (System.Devices.InterfaceClassGuid:="{...}" AND
  System.Devices.InterfaceEnabled:=...Boolean#True) for the capture, render
  and camera classes.
- DefaultAudioCaptureDeviceChanged and DefaultAudioRenderDeviceChanged
  keep their handlers under unique tokens (referenced until removed;
  NULL token E_POINTER, NULL handler E_INVALIDARG; removing an unknown
  token is S_OK). They are not raised yet.
- DllGetActivationFactory hands out the factory only for
  Windows.Media.Devices.MediaDevice (any name used to get it);
  DllGetClassObject has no FIXME. GetDefault*Id checks its out pointer
  and the allocation.

---
